      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Prosthetic voice rehabilitation post-laryngectomy is becoming more popular with otolaryngologists in Canada. However, as with any procedure, surgeons must be aware of potential complications. We present the first detailed report of a case in the creation of a dissecting false passage following tracheoesophageal puncture."},
